win64 (LLP64) build of HG/SS (hwin1): what Linux's LP64 build hides.
- `#ifdef __LP64__` as the 64-bit-host test (src/system.c's V-blank task queue: 256 on a host, 32 on the DS; port/asmdata's
  PORT_OVYID, an overlay id in a static initializer) is false on win64: the queue was the DS's 32 there and the asm data
  copies failed to compile (a truncated address is no constant). Now `__LP64__ || _WIN64`.
- ov44's three overlay functions were declared to return int (two take int *) where overlay_44_02232E9C.h says s32 (long on
  win64's libntr types).
- ov12_02238A68.c's own `typedef long time_t` (and time()'s prototype, unused) clash with MinGW's 64-bit time_t.
- (The narrow-prototype fixes that were here, sub_0200FF88's screen and sub_0200EA24's sizes, are in the decomp itself since
  hgss-port f60356cfd: declarations equal definitions, which tools/hg_abi_scan.py lists the rest of.)
